####################################################################################################
# VERNIER-26 -- DOES THE LOOP SHARPEN THE BACKGROUND MEASUREMENT?
# EXPLORATORY, NOT PRE-REGISTERED.  Fourier-domain estimators only.
####################################################################################################
  array 116 pulsars, sigma_toa(med) 100 ns, T = 20 yr, 1/T = 1.584 nHz
  band 7.92-30.10 nHz in 15 bins; GWB/white per bin 5.2 -> 0.02 (crossing inside the band)
  sky: VERNIER-24 Arm B, Pareto gamma_eff = 1.56, 300 explicit per bin + HD-correlated faint sea
  A_true = 2.400e-15, gamma_true = 4.3333, r_P = 1.196, Earth-coherent fraction q = 0.411, realisations = 200
  measured HD-filter calibration against the regularised antenna response: k = 1.0474 (divided out; a constant, so it cancels in every difference)

  realised sky: median lambda_fore = 0.309, faint-sea fraction (below top 300) = 8.24 % of the bin
  N_bin 1.61e+05 (7.9 nHz) -> 1.21e+03 (30 nHz)

====================================================================================================
CONTROL 0 -- PURE-NOISE NULL (no GWB, no sources, nothing to find)
====================================================================================================
  A^2 / A^2_true (auto)    mean -0.0021  sd 0.0188  median -0.0024
  A^2 / A^2_true (cross)   mean -0.0008  sd 0.0184  median -0.0003
  OS SNR                   mean -0.0102  sd 0.2411  median -0.0039
  -> OS SNR null -0.010 +- 0.241 (s.e. of the mean 0.017): the MEAN is consistent with zero, so
     the estimator does not manufacture a correlation. The SPREAD is 0.24 and not 1 because the
     weights P_a = pw_a + S_model assume a background the null does not contain -- the SNR column
     is therefore CONSERVATIVE by ~4.1x in the no-signal limit, and is only ever compared across treatments.

