DELIVERABLE 3 -- THE M-C COLUMN: the HD variance floor set by the
  pulsar terms. sigma_A/A of the OPTIMALLY weighted HD amplitude,
  computed from the per-pulsar residual SIGNAL power. Pulsar terms
  enter here and nowhere else, so (ii) -> (iii) is M-C alone.
====================================================================================================
    R |  floor (i)  (ii) earth  (iii) cond  (iii-s) scr |  M-C gain    HAZARD |  pterm frac
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    0 |    0.02424           -           -            - |         -         - |           -
    4 |    0.02424     0.02284     0.01779      0.02354 |   +23.75%    -3.01% |      96.63%
    8 |    0.02424     0.02223     0.01653      0.02317 |   +27.12%    -4.23% |     124.62%
   16 |    0.02424     0.02164     0.01550      0.02284 |   +29.72%    -5.49% |     146.48%
   25 |    0.02424     0.02125     0.01491      0.02248 |   +31.12%    -5.75% |     169.33%

  M-C gain = PAIRED mean of 1 - floor(iii)/floor(ii): the fraction of
             the HD variance floor that certified distances remove.
  HAZARD   = the same for SCRAMBLED distances. It must be ~0 (or
             negative) or the M-C claim is void (ORACLE rule S5.5.1).
  pterm frac = MEDIAN over bins/realisations of the pulsar-term power
             of the recovered sources, as a fraction of the residual
             background they sit in. The mean is far larger and is
             not quotable: the Pareto tail makes it unstable.

