DELIVERABLE 4 -- MECHANISM ATTRIBUTION, all paired
====================================================================================================
    R | M-A bias(ii) M-A bias(iii) M-A removed | M-B var i->ii | M-C floor   HAZARD
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4 |      +0.1029       -0.0154     +0.1182 |         -4.9% |   +23.75%   -3.01%
    8 |      +0.1678       -0.0228     +0.1906 |         -7.9% |   +27.12%   -4.23%
   16 |      +0.2507       -0.0327     +0.2834 |        -31.8% |   +29.72%   -5.49%
   25 |      +0.3274       -0.0438     +0.3712 |        -39.6% |   +31.12%   -5.75%

  M-A = residual bias of the CRN/AUTO amplitude. Under (ii) the
        recovered sources' PULSAR terms are still in the data and
        are pure excess auto power; under (iii) they are gone.
        'M-A removed' is what modelling them buys, in units of the
        residual background itself.
  M-B = fractional drop in RMSE of the reconstructed TOTAL amp^2
        (cross estimator) on moving from unmodelled to Earth-
        subtracted, i.e. what reassignment alone buys.

